(That header is about THIS FILE, which is a licence pointer — repository
metadata, like the other per-directory LICENSE files, so it carries the same
MIT OR Apache-2.0 as they do and REUSE.toml lists it with them. What it says
about the directory's contents is below.)

Everything in assets/ that was made for this project — voxel models (.vox),
textures, sound effects and music — is licensed under

  Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
  (../LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt)

CC BY-SA 4.0 is one-way compatible with GPLv3: these assets can be shipped
inside the GPL-3.0-or-later game, but GPL'd material cannot be relicensed back
into them. To reuse an asset you must give attribution ("Pharmakos
contributors", CC BY-SA 4.0, with a link to the licence and a note of any
changes) and share your adaptation under CC BY-SA 4.0 or a compatible licence.

THIRD-PARTY ASSETS ARE NOT COVERED BY THIS FILE. Anything sourced from
elsewhere keeps its own copyright and licence, recorded in a sidecar file next
to it — `foo.ogg.license` beside `foo.ogg` — naming the author, the source URL,
the licence and any changes made. Audio may only come from CC0 or CC-BY
sources; Sonniss GDC bundles are excluded. See ../docs/LICENSING.md for the
sourcing rule and the credits-screen requirement.

Unless you state otherwise, any contribution you intentionally submit for
inclusion in this directory shall be licensed as above, with no additional
terms or conditions, and signed off under the Developer Certificate of Origin
1.1 (../docs/DCO.txt).

The repository-wide scheme is described in ../LICENSE; the machine-readable
manifest is ../REUSE.toml.
